// Title: Remote Access Tool - AnyDesk Silent Installation
// Sigma ID: 114e7f1c-f137-48c8-8f54-3088c24ce4b9
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Ján Trenčanský
// Date: 2021-08-06 | Modified: 2023-03-05
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1219.002
// Description: Detects AnyDesk Remote Desktop silent installation. Which can be used by attackers to gain
//   remote access.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate deployment of AnyDesk
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/TheDFIRReport/status/1423361119926816776?s=20
//   - https://support.anydesk.com/Automatic_Deployment
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_anydesk_silent_install.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "--install" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--start-with-win" and ProcessCommandLine contains "--silent"
